                    },
                    "message": "Do not sprinkle pragmas around the codebase.  Fix the issues or don't use the tools."
                },
                {
                    "file": "apphandler.cpp",
                    "line": 528,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "correct change is to make str a proper string instead of a string_view. \n\nThe error message is saying that once m[matches[0]].str() finishes executing (and assigning to the string_view), it will deconstruct, which means that the string_view will be left with dangling references to a string that doesn't exist. By making str a std::string, it will keep that string alive while it is being used.\n\nSame goes for the other matches below."
                },
